{"term":"dwarf","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:def6c73c35205d4586","definition":"Any member of a race of beings from (especially Scandinavian and other Germanic) folklore, usually depicted as having some sort of supernatural powers and being skilled in crafting and metalworking, often as short with long beards, and sometimes as clashing with elves.","example":"[T]he elf king and his queen made a royal progress every noon with a splendid retinue of dwarves and sprites, […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["dwarfin","dwarrow"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bedwarf","bullet dwarf","durgan","durgy","dwarfage","dwarfdom","dwarfen","dwarven","Dwarfer","dwarfess","dwarfette","dwarf-hill","dwarf holder","dwarf-holder","dwarfify","dwarfish","dwarvish","dwarfism","dwarfkind","dwarflike","dwarfling","dwarfmaid","dwarfness","dwarf signal","dwarfsploitation","dwarf standing on the shoulders of giants","dwarf tossing","dwarf wall","dwarfy","dwelf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dwarf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8ea09f0ac6f964b5e6","definition":"A person of short stature, often one whose limbs are disproportionately small in relation to the body as compared with typical adults, usually as the result of a genetic condition.","example":"The nurse exclaimed it when I finally arrived, a month late (a habit I have kept). That's how my parents found out that I was a little person, a dwarf, of short stature.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["elf","midget","pygmy"],"antonyms":["ettin","giant"],"collocations":[],"usage":"offensive, sometimes","register":"offensive, sometimes","wordFamily":["bedwarf","bullet dwarf","durgan","durgy","dwarfage","dwarfdom","dwarfen","dwarven","Dwarfer","dwarfess","dwarfette","dwarf-hill","dwarf holder","dwarf-holder","dwarfify","dwarfish","dwarvish","dwarfism","dwarfkind","dwarflike","dwarfling","dwarfmaid","dwarfness","dwarf signal","dwarfsploitation","dwarf standing on the shoulders of giants","dwarf tossing","dwarf wall","dwarfy","dwelf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dwarf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b7436cdd93005a6c5a","definition":"An animal, plant or other thing much smaller than the usual of its sort.","example":"dwarf tree","pos":"noun","synonyms":["runt"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bedwarf","bullet dwarf","durgan","durgy","dwarfage","dwarfdom","dwarfen","dwarven","Dwarfer","dwarfess","dwarfette","dwarf-hill","dwarf holder","dwarf-holder","dwarfify","dwarfish","dwarvish","dwarfism","dwarfkind","dwarflike","dwarfling","dwarfmaid","dwarfness","dwarf signal","dwarfsploitation","dwarf standing on the shoulders of giants","dwarf tossing","dwarf wall","dwarfy","dwelf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dwarf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eebba4bb9bf7a52adf","definition":"A dwarf star.","example":"But none of those brown dwarfs were speeding along on a trajectory that would carry them out of the galaxy like “runaway” hypervelocity stars observed by astronomers in the last two decades. […] The study team said it’s likely the star was a companion to a white dwarf star, which is the remaining core of a dead star that has expelled the gases that serve as its nuclear fuel.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bedwarf","bullet dwarf","durgan","durgy","dwarfage","dwarfdom","dwarfen","dwarven","Dwarfer","dwarfess","dwarfette","dwarf-hill","dwarf holder","dwarf-holder","dwarfify","dwarfish","dwarvish","dwarfism","dwarfkind","dwarflike","dwarfling","dwarfmaid","dwarfness","dwarf signal","dwarfsploitation","dwarf standing on the sho